                          <node index="0" text="This is f*cking insane. Former Google CEO Eric Schmidt just said the quiet part about making money with AI:&#10;&#10;&quot;If you really want to make money, it's actually easy. Found an agentic AI company. Build an agent to do something&#10;&#10;If you build a better agent than anyone else, you can probably build one incredible company and own it yourself&quot;&#10;&#10;In 27 seconds, the man who ran Google for 10 years explains why the next 1-2 years are the agentic window, and why it closes fast&#10;&#10;Idea → Fable 5.2 → One Agent → Harness → Loops → A Company You Own&#10;&#10;Everything below is free:&#10;&#10;Building effective agents, Anthropic's playbook&#10;anthropic.com/research/build…&#10;&#10;How Anthropic built its multi-agent research system&#10;anthropic.com/research/multi…&#10;&#10;Harnesses for agents that run for days&#10;anthropic.com/research/effec…&#10;&#10;Writing tools your agent can actually use&#10;anthropic.com/research/writi…&#10;&#10;Claude Agent SDK, the stack Anthropic builds on&#10;code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-…&#10;&#10;Claude Code best practices&#10;code.claude.com/docs/en/best-p…&#10;&#10;Subagents: run the work in parallel&#10;code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-ag…&#10;&#10;Hooks: checks your agent can't skip&#10;code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks&#10;&#10;Skills: teach it a job once&#10;code.claude.com/docs/en/skills&#10;&#10;Claude Code in Action, free hands-on course&#10;anthropic.skilljar.com/claude-code-in…&#10;&#10;12-factor agents: rules for agents that don't break&#10;github.com/humanlayer/12-…&#10;&#10;LangGraph: graphs of agents&#10;github.com/langchain-ai/l…&#10;&#10;Karpathy's autoresearch: an agent in a loop&#10;github.com/karpathy/autor…&#10;&#10;Claude cookbooks: recipes you can copy tonight&#10;github.com/anthropics/cla…&#10;&#10;Total: $0&#10;&#10;99% will spend the agentic window scrolling threads about agents. The 1% who ship one will own what comes out of it&#10;&#10;Bookmark it and open the first link tonight&#10;&#10;Then read how to build an agent that runs for hours without you in the harness, loops and graphs guide below ↓" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.twitter.android" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" visible-to-user="true" bounds="[22,0][1047,1478]" drawing-order="0" hint="" display-id="0"/>
